  "id": "motor-scale",
  "term": "Motor scale",
  "definition": "A motor scale is a structured measure used to assess motor functioning by rating a person’s ability to perform movement-related activities and the amount of assistance needed. In this source, it refers to a smaller gross motor scale developed for people with Rett syndrome, with items grouped into general motor skills and more complex gross motor skills.",
